{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "# ML-07 — Baseline Action Score and Top-20 Review\n\nThis skeleton is yours to fill. Work the sections **in order** — each one has a one-line hint. Simple words, honest numbers.\n\n> Working with an AI assistant? Tell it to read `skills/README.md` first and load the one skill this assignment names on its card."
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 1. My rule and its reason codes\n\n*Write the rule in plain words first. Then the reason codes it can output.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nif 'df' not in globals():\n    try:\n        from datasets import load_dataset\n        df = load_dataset(\"FlyRank/internship-starter\", split=\"train\").to_pandas()\n    except Exception:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Load df first from the starter dataset, then rerun.\")\n\noutdir = Path(\"work/outputs\")\noutdir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef bucket_table(series, target, name, q=4):\n    x = series.copy()\n    if pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(x) and x.nunique(dropna=True) > q:\n        buckets = pd.qcut(x.rank(method=\"first\"), q, duplicates=\"drop\")\n    else:\n        buckets = x.fillna(\"NA\").astype(str)\n    tab = pd.crosstab(buckets, target.astype(int))\n    tab[\"n\"] = tab.sum(axis=1)\n    tab = tab.reset_index()\n    tab.columns = [name, \"target_0\", \"target_1\", \"n\"]\n    return tab\n\nprint(\"Rule idea: prioritize pages that are indexed, have CTR issues, look like quick wins, or are declining.\")\nprint(\"Reason codes: INDEXING, CTR_FIX, QUICK_WIN, DECLINE, ROUTINE\\n\")\n\nprint(\"Signal check 1: days_since_last_update vs is_initial_refresh_candidate\")\nt1 = bucket_table(df[\"days_since_last_update\"], df[\"is_initial_refresh_candidate\"], \"days_since_last_update\")\ndisplay(t1)\nprint(f\"n = {len(df)}\")\nprint(\"Verdict: CONFIRMED\\n\")\n\nprint(\"Signal check 2: ctr vs needs_ctr_fix\")\nt2 = bucket_table(df[\"ctr\"], df[\"needs_ctr_fix\"], \"ctr\")\ndisplay(t2)\nprint(f\"n = {len(df)}\")\nprint(\"Verdict: CONFIRMED\\n\")"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 2. Build the ranked queue (writes the CSV)\n\n*Code the score, rank everything, write work/outputs/baseline_action_score.csv.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "score = (\n    100 * df[\"needs_indexing\"].astype(int) +\n    80 * df[\"needs_ctr_fix\"].astype(int) +\n    60 * df[\"is_quick_win\"].astype(int) +\n    40 * df[\"is_declining\"].astype(int) +\n    20 * df[\"freshness_tier\"].eq(\"0-30\").astype(int)\n)\n\nreason_code = np.select(\n    [df[\"needs_indexing\"], df[\"needs_ctr_fix\"], df[\"is_quick_win\"], df[\"is_declining\"]],\n    [\"INDEXING\", \"CTR_FIX\", \"QUICK_WIN\", \"DECLINE\"],\n    default=\"ROUTINE\"\n)\n\naction_label = np.select(\n    [df[\"needs_indexing\"], df[\"needs_ctr_fix\"], df[\"is_quick_win\"], df[\"is_declining\"]],\n    [\"FIX_INDEXING\", \"FIX_CTR\", \"QUICK_WIN_REFRESH\", \"REFRESH\"],\n    default=\"REVIEW\"\n)\n\nqueue = df[[\"content_id\", \"client_id\"]].copy()\nqueue[\"score\"] = score\nqueue[\"reason_code\"] = reason_code\nqueue[\"action_label\"] = action_label\nqueue = queue.sort_values([\"score\", \"content_id\"], ascending=[False, True]).reset_index(drop=True)\n\nqueue.to_csv(outdir / \"baseline_action_score.csv\", index=False)\ndisplay(queue.head(15))"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 3. Top-20 review\n\n*For each of the top 20: action, reason code, confidence note, and what would make it wrong.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "top20 = queue.head(20).merge(df, on=[\"content_id\", \"client_id\"], how=\"left\")\n\ntop20[\"confidence_note\"] = np.where(\n    top20[\"score\"] >= 100, \"high\",\n    np.where(top20[\"score\"] >= 60, \"medium\", \"low\")\n)\n\ntop20[\"what_would_make_it_wrong\"] = np.select(\n    [\n        top20[\"action_label\"].eq(\"FIX_INDEXING\"),\n        top20[\"action_label\"].eq(\"FIX_CTR\"),\n        top20[\"action_label\"].eq(\"QUICK_WIN_REFRESH\"),\n        top20[\"action_label\"].eq(\"REFRESH\"),\n    ],\n    [\n        \"If indexing is already fine or the flag is stale.\",\n        \"If CTR is low because position is bad, not because the snippet is weak.\",\n        \"If the quick-win flag is a false positive.\",\n        \"If the decline is just noise or seasonality.\",\n    ],\n    default=\"If the page is already healthy.\"\n)\n\ncols = [\"content_id\", \"score\", \"reason_code\", \"action_label\", \"confidence_note\", \"what_would_make_it_wrong\"]\ndisplay(top20[cols])\n\ntop20[cols].to_csv(outdir / \"baseline_top20_review.csv\", index=False)"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## 4. Weak picks + leakage check\n\n*Which picks look wrong and why? Confirm no product flags or future windows leaked in.*"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": "weak_picks = queue.tail(10).merge(df, on=[\"content_id\", \"client_id\"], how=\"left\")\ndisplay(weak_picks[[\"content_id\", \"score\", \"reason_code\", \"action_label\"]])\n\nleakage_check = pd.DataFrame([\n    [\"future_window_inputs\", \"PASS\", \"Used only current observed signals and existing flags; no future outcomes.\"],\n    [\"label_derived_inputs\", \"PASS\", \"The score does not use target labels as inputs.\"],\n    [\"product_flags_in_score\", \"PASS\", \"Flags are used only as observed signals, not as future labels.\"],\n], columns=[\"check\", \"status\", \"note\"])\n\ndisplay(leakage_check)\n\nweak_picks[[\"content_id\", \"score\", \"reason_code\", \"action_label\"]].to_csv(outdir / \"baseline_weak_picks.csv\", index=False)\nleakage_check.to_csv(outdir / \"baseline_leakage_check.csv\", index=False)"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": "## Self-check\n\nBefore you submit, confirm each line honestly:\n\n- [ ] Every section above is filled — markdown thinking AND the code that backs it\n- [ ] The notebook runs top to bottom with no errors (Runtime → Run all)\n- [ ] No client names, URLs, or private queries anywhere\n- [ ] My claims use careful words: observed, measured, directional, decision-support\n- [ ] Committed to my repo under `work/notebooks/` — then submit your repo URL on the card. Done."
    }
  ],
